I'm gonna demonstrate that in just a second.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.680
the other breakthrough

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.575
is that there are new standards

00:09:41.575 --> 00:09:45.875
that communicate uncertainties as auditable data.

00:09:45.875 --> 00:09:48.945
And that has led to the discipline of probability management,

00:09:48.945 --> 00:09:51.945
which I'll be describing a little bit further.

00:09:51.945 --> 00:09:54.205
It's a simple idea, that is,

00:09:54.205 --> 00:10:00.905
uncertainties are modeled as any other kind of data, auditable data.

00:10:00.905 --> 00:10:03.435
Now, I wanna point out here that

00:10:03.435 --> 00:10:05.005
this is really the most important,

00:10:05.005 --> 00:10:06.500
message of the webinar,

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.980
that due to these two breakthroughs, anyone,

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:19.320
anywhere with Excel can be curing the Flaw of Averages.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.330
So let me demonstrate this using dice.

