So, remember shaking the ladder

00:55:53.695 --> 00:55:57.420
close counts with horseshoes,

00:55:57.420 --> 00:56:00.615
hand grenades, and simulation.

00:56:00.615 --> 00:56:05.620
And by the way, there are some recent advances that really help us,

00:56:05.620 --> 00:56:10.130
turn data into SIP libraries. It's very exciting.

00:56:10.130 --> 00:56:12.890
I'm working with some colleagues on that

00:56:12.890 --> 00:56:17.525
now and we'll certainly spend plenty of time on that.

00:56:17.525 --> 00:56:21.755
but we also have to get you

00:56:21.755 --> 00:56:26.845
basically over the hump of doing it with very little data.

00:56:26.845 --> 00:56:29.405
Don't get blocked by that.

00:56:29.405 --> 00:56:32.185
Oh, I'll just say one last thing about this.

00:56:32.185 --> 00:56:35.105
Some people say, "Oh no, no, I couldn't,

00:56:35.105 --> 00:56:38.760
I couldn't simulate anything because I don't have enough data," right?

00:56:38.760 --> 00:56:40.555
If you don't have enough data,

00:56:40.555 --> 00:56:41.880
that means you are very,

00:56:41.880 --> 00:56:43.705
very uncertain about what's going on.

00:56:43.705 --> 00:56:48.080
So, saying "I couldn't do analysis because I don't have enough data" is like

00:56:48.080 --> 00:56:50.030
